From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marcho78 <marcho78@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: tegra: dfll: Hold CPU speedo 2 below 2218.5 MHz for the
 SHIELD TV 2017

The DFLL builds its OPP table, and so cpufreq's rates, up to
tegra210_cpu_max_freq_table[speedo_id]. For speedo 2 that is 2218.5 MHz,
above the 2014.5 MHz the SHIELD TV 2017's (SKU 0x87) stock kernel uses.
While the DFLL is brought up on that board, the limit goes up in stages:
1020 MHz (the CVB table's rate closest to the 1017.6 MHz cboot leaves
pll_x at), then 1912.5 MHz, then stock's 2014.5 MHz.

Not for upstream: a bring-up limit for darcy (NOTES.md).
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c b/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
index 457a77c5b..5bb789472 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
@@ -175,7 +175,11 @@ static const struct cvb_table tegra124_cpu_cvb_tables[] = {
 static const unsigned long tegra210_cpu_max_freq_table[] = {
 	[0] = 1912500000UL,
 	[1] = 1912500000UL,
-	[2] = 2218500000UL,
+	/*
+	 * The SHIELD TV 2017 (SKU 0x87) is speedo 2, and its stock kernel
+	 * stops at 2014500000. Held at 1912500000 while its DFLL is brought up.
+	 */
+	[2] = 1912500000UL,
 	[3] = 1785000000UL,
 	[4] = 1632000000UL,
 	[5] = 1912500000UL,
